IMPORT prelude

§ `Set operations`

-- "residents of New York and New Jersey may apply"
-- SET OF collects two-or-more arguments; equivalent to setFromList (LIST ...)
`new yorkers`   MEANS SET OF "alice", "bob"
-- a SINGLE element can't use bare SET OF (one argument is read as the
-- contents list); use setFromList or SET OF LIST for singletons
`new jerseyans` MEANS setFromList (LIST "carol")

-- term-level AND on sets is union: three people are eligible
`eligible` MEANS `new yorkers` AND `new jerseyans`
#EVAL setSize `eligible`                                   -- 3
#EVAL "carol" `is in` `eligible`                           -- TRUE

-- sentence-level AND on booleans is still conjunction
#EVAL TRUE AND FALSE                                       -- FALSE

§§ `The canonical vocabulary`

#EVAL setSize (`new yorkers` UNION `new jerseyans`)        -- 3
#EVAL setSize (`new yorkers` INTERSECT `new jerseyans`)    -- 0

-- difference: LESS wears backticks (bare LESS starts LESS THAN);
-- WITHOUT is the bare-spelling alias
`all employees` MEANS setFromList (LIST "dilbert", "alice", "wally", "asok")
`on probation`  MEANS setFromList (LIST "asok")
#EVAL setSize (`all employees` `LESS` `on probation`)      -- 3
#EVAL setSize (`all employees` WITHOUT `on probation`)     -- 3

§§ `PLUS and MINUS: bare, with real precedence`

a1 MEANS setFromList (LIST 1, 2, 3)
b1 MEANS setFromList (LIST 2, 3, 4)

#EVAL setSize (a1 PLUS b1)                                 -- 4  (union)
#EVAL setSize (a1 MINUS b1)                                -- 1  (difference)
-- chains need no parentheses, but beware: not a group!
#EVAL setToList (a1 PLUS b1 MINUS b1)                      -- LIST 1, not a1

§§ `Equality is extensional — via set equals`

#EVAL (setFromList (LIST 2, 1, 1)) `set equals` (setFromList (LIST 1, 2))   -- TRUE

§§ `Enums make good elements`

DECLARE State IS ONE OF NY, NJ, CT

`the tri-state universe` MEANS setFromList (LIST NY, NJ, CT)
`eligible states`        MEANS setFromList (LIST NY, NJ)

#EVAL CT `is in` `eligible states`                         -- FALSE
-- absolute complement, since the enum universe is finite
#EVAL setToList (`the tri-state universe` WITHOUT `eligible states`)   -- LIST CT
